# Git Workflow

## Branches

- Primary: `main`
- Feature work: short-lived branches (repo often uses `cursor/<topic>`)
- Prefer PR merges into `main`; avoid force-push to `main`

## Commits (hybrid)

Prefer Conventional Commits (already common in history):

```
feat(scope): summary
fix(scope): summary
docs: summary
test: summary
chore: summary
```

Scopes used in practice: `lsp`, `ai`, `terminal`, `editor`, etc.

Version bumps are explicit commits (`Bump version to x.y.z.`) from `scripts/release.ps1`.

## Releases

```powershell
pwsh scripts/release.ps1           # patch bump default
pwsh scripts/release.ps1 -Bump minor
pwsh scripts/release.ps1 -Version 1.0.0
pwsh scripts/release.ps1 -DryRun
```

Tag push triggers `.github/workflows/release.yml` (artifacts + GitHub Release; optional Store MSIX when Partner Center secrets are set).

## PRs

- Summarize user-facing behavior and test plan
- Run `dotnet test` before considering the change complete
- Sync `AGENTS.md` / `README.md` when scripts, deps, or workflows change

---
**Hybrid:** existing branch/release flow + conventional commit discipline
